## 1. Definitions

### 1.1 Work

The **"Work"** means the entire project or work to which this license is applied and all associated portions of it, including but not limited to:

* source and compiled code;
* assets and media;
* data and configuration files;
* documentation and text;
* project and resource files; and
* other material distributed as part of or for use with the Work.

A portion of the Work remains subject to this license when copied, extracted, modified, incorporated into another project, or redistributed separately.

Separating, extracting, converting, recompiling, repackaging, renaming, or otherwise changing the form of any portion of the Work does not remove that portion from this license.

### 1.2 Modified Work

A **"Modified Work"** means the Work, or any portion of the Work, that has been modified, adapted, translated, converted, expanded, reduced, or otherwise altered.

### 1.3 Original Author

The **"Original Author"** or **"Original Authors"** means electikos and any other author or creator identified as an original author of the Work or an applicable portion of the Work.

### 1.4 NSFW Content

**"NSFW Content"** means content that is sexually explicit, pornographic, fetishistic, or primarily intended for sexual arousal.

This includes, but is not limited to:

* explicit sexual acts or depictions of sexual activity;
* exposed genitalia presented in a sexual context;
* sexualized nudity;
* pornographic or erotic material; and
* fetish content presented for sexual gratification.

Non-sexual artistic, educational, medical, or anatomical content is not considered NSFW Content solely because it contains nudity.

### 1.5 Artificial Intelligence and Generative AI

**"Artificial Intelligence" ("AI")** includes machine-learning-based systems used to analyze, generate, transform, modify, reconstruct, or assist in creating content.

**"Generative AI"** means an AI system capable of generating or substantially transforming code, text, images, audio, video, models, data, or other material.

### 1.6 Contribution

A **"Contribution"** means any code, asset, documentation, data, media, patch, modification, pull request, submission, or other material intentionally submitted for inclusion in, improvement of, or use with the Work.

### 1.7 Official Project Hosts

**"Official Project Hosts"** means the public websites, repositories, distribution platforms, project pages, or other public locations identified by the Original Author in the file **`PROJECT_HOSTS.md`** distributed with the Work.

Examples may include an official source repository, CurseForge project page, Modrinth project page, or another officially designated distribution location.

A mirror, fork, repost, archive, or other location not listed in `PROJECT_HOSTS.md` is not an Official Project Host for purposes of this license.

### 1.8 Project Inactivity

**"Project Inactivity"** means a period during which no new version, release, build, package, file, or other update of the Work has been uploaded or published by or on behalf of the Original Author to any Official Project Host listed in `PROJECT_HOSTS.md`.

Project Inactivity is measured from the date of the most recent qualifying upload or publication to an Official Project Host.

Commits, private development activity, announcements, discussions, issue activity, pull requests, or other activity that does not result in an upload or publication of the Work to an Official Project Host do not reset the inactivity period.

An upload or publication to any Official Project Host listed in `PROJECT_HOSTS.md` resets the inactivity period.

