## 4. Obligations When Distributing a Modified Work

If you distribute a Modified Work or a modified portion of the Work, you must:

1. Preserve the name or pseudonym of the Original Author(s) and provide appropriate attribution.

2. Clearly state that the Work or applicable portion has been modified.

3. Include a complete copy of this license with the distributed Modified Work.

4. Distribute portions derived from the Work under the **Electron Non-Commercial License (ENCL-2)**.

5. Preserve original author attribution contained in the Work or accompanying materials.

6. Preserve the original `PROJECT_HOSTS.md` file so that the Original Author's Official Project Hosts remain identifiable.

7. Comply with the AI and Generative AI disclosure requirements in Section 5 when applicable.

---

## 5. AI and Generative AI Use Disclosure

AI and Generative AI may be used to modify the Work. However, their use must be disclosed when a Modified Work is distributed.

If AI or Generative AI was used to create, modify, transform, reconstruct, or substantially assist with any portion of the distributed Modified Work, the distributor must clearly disclose:

1. **The affected files or portions of the Work.**
   Identify the files, assets, components, or other portions that were created or modified with AI assistance.

2. **The AI product or service used.**
   Identify the application, service, program, or platform through which the AI was used.

3. **The AI model used.**
   Identify the model, model family, or model version used where that information is known or made available by the product or service.

If the exact model or model version is not made available to the user, the distributor must identify the product or service used and state that the exact model was not provided or could not be determined.

The disclosure must be reasonably accessible with the Modified Work, such as in its documentation, credits, README, changelog, or other accompanying material.

A disclosure may group multiple files together when the same AI product and model were used for the same type of modification, provided the affected files or portions can still be reasonably identified.

The use of AI does not remove or reduce any attribution, licensing, content, or redistribution requirement imposed by this license.

