## 7. Public Forks and Third-Party Republishing

A private fork or private modified copy may be created at any time, subject to this license.

A **public fork**, public redistribution of a fork, or publication of the Work or a Modified Work on a public distribution platform may occur without separate permission from the Original Author.

The inactivity period begins on the date of the most recent qualifying upload or publication of the Work to any Official Project Host listed in `PROJECT_HOSTS.md`.

Any later qualifying upload or publication by or on behalf of the Original Author to any Official Project Host resets the inactivity period to zero.

For purposes of this section, qualifying activity is limited to an actual upload or publication of the Work, a release, build, package, file, or updated version of the Work to an Official Project Host.

The following do **not** reset the inactivity period unless they are accompanied by a qualifying upload or publication:

* source-control commits;
* branch activity;
* issue or pull-request activity;
* announcements;
* comments or discussions;
* development screenshots;
* private builds;
* private testing; or
* statements that development is continuing.

Once the required inactivity period has elapsed, a person may publicly fork or republish the Work or a Modified Work, including on platforms such as CurseForge or Modrinth, provided all other requirements of this license are followed.

A permitted public fork or republication must:

1. clearly identify itself as an unofficial fork, continuation, or modified version;

2. not represent itself as the original or official project;

3. preserve attribution to the Original Author(s);

4. preserve the original `PROJECT_HOSTS.md`;

5. provide a reasonable link or reference to the original Work or an Official Project Host when one remains publicly available; and

6. continue to comply with all other terms of this license.

A public fork or republication does not become an Official Project Host merely because it is publicly available.

